    "attribution": "ORIGINATING_ERROR",
    "criticism": "Step 8 introduced a new error by attempting to scrape the Met Museum’s collection page with an incorrect URL pattern and HTML selectors. The accession number 29.100.5 is not directly accessible via the simple \"search/{accession_number}\" endpoint, and the page’s HTML structure does not contain elements with classes 'card__title', 'card__artist', 'card__date', or 'card__description'. Consequently, the BeautifulSoup calls returned None, and the subsequent get_text() calls would raise exceptions or silently fail, resulting in no output. Because this step failed to retrieve any portrait information, it prevented the Church Historian from identifying the subject and the later steps from determining the consecrators. A correct version would use the Met’s official search API or the proper URL format (e.g., https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/12345) and parse the actual page elements (such as the title in an <h1> tag and the artist name in a <span> with class \"artistName\"). Additionally, adding error handling to report missing elements would prevent silent failures."
